WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.458
A shield blocked

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.720
Java4Shell without

00:00:02.532 --> 00:00:03.392
a restart

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.462
OpenAI and Cisco

00:00:05.274 --> 00:00:06.677
are launching Shirudo

00:00:06.878 --> 00:00:08.293
an open-source runtime

00:00:08.104 --> 00:00:09.224
that protects running

00:00:09.036 --> 00:00:10.274
Linux systems while

00:00:10.085 --> 00:00:11.087
teams roll out

00:00:10.899 --> 00:00:11.712
patches

00:00:12.238 --> 00:00:13.558
It uses eBPF

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.454
to block vulnerable

00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:15.480
code paths live

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.598
In a controlled

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:16.999
test

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:18.921
a Codex-generated shield

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:20.442
stopped a Java4Shell

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:21.409
exploit against a

00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:22.494
running Elasticsearch

00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:22.989
service

00:00:23.096 --> 00:00:24.416
with no restart

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.612
Shields are cryptographically

00:00:26.424 --> 00:00:27.084
signed

00:00:27.273 --> 00:00:28.086
checked by the

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:29.572
eBPF verifier

00:00:29.643 --> 00:00:30.551
and logged with

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.258
a TPM

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.048
It's BSD licensed

00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:33.956
and a technical

00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:34.982
webinar follows on

00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:36.102
December 15

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.644
Full story on

00:00:37.455 --> 00:00:38.351
the dashboard
